From 09df279fe0d2a78924361117f89d3933acc49349 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 22:08:23 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 11132/11362] [outer-loop] Record two measured nulls and
 correct three mis-stated flag states

Operator-authorized. The ledger read 136 unevaluated and 0 off_measured, so no
measured null had ever been recorded and the dashboard reported flags as
shipped-but-untested that had in fact been tested.

Two external nulls recorded with evidence paths and sha256, from the paired
cd82/r11l runs: CARNOT_ARC_INDUCE_TOOL_LOOP and CARNOT_ARC_SUPERVISOR_TOOL_ARM.
Both arms fire and change nothing measurable. The supervisor arm carries a note
that the window defaulting to the action budget is a separate defect and does
not turn its null into a positive.

Three entries carried state: unevaluated alongside last_measured 2026-08-14 and
a full REFUSED verdict naming the games each flag regressed. That state was
simply wrong: they were measured, and they lost. Migrated to off_measured with
every verdict preserved, so the distinction between 'no benefit' and 'broke
bp35 and cd82' stays readable in the record.

Rejected: the aggressive rule that would migrate 15 entries. Only the three
with an explicit measured verdict were touched.

Dashboard now reads 2/4 shipped-but-untested rather than 4/4.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JntPrUGLNesPcJH1pyfFYw
